## How I work

A note on my working style, since it shapes how I approach analysis:

- **I break ambiguous work into a concrete first action.** When a task feels
  hard to start, the blocker is usually an unclear next step — so I begin with
  something small and concrete rather than planning the whole thing first.
- **I learn by doing, then fill gaps as they appear** — starting from hands-on
  problems and looking things up when I get stuck.
- **I reflect on my own process and iterate on it**, the same way I'd iterate on
  an analysis.
